> Notice that Windows should go to the upper branch. I have no idea why the else branch was triggered, a quick fix is to remove that branch.

This can be caused by nvcc, not MSVC. I guess we need something like `#if defined(_WIN32) || defined(__WIN32__)` to guard it.

When building an extension, we can do a quick fix like https://github.com/woct0rdho/SageAttention/commit/914fe0ed304c3db4a27735d394ae23c5d5e79701 :
```python3
if os.name == "nt":
    NVCC_FLAGS += [
        "-D_WIN32=1",
        "-DUSE_CUDA=1",
    ]
```

Or if it's preferable to modify the source before building, we can comment out the following lines in `torch/include/torch/csrc/dynamo/compiled_autograd.h`:
```cpp
    } else if constexpr (::std::is_same_v<T, ::std::string>) {
      return at::StringType::get();
```

This issue still exists as of torch 2.10.0 .
